Only include <BaseTsd.h> where it is used (MSVC), so mingw can build

`src/utils.h` includes <BaseTsd.h> unconditionally under _WIN32, but the only
symbol it takes from that header is SSIZE_T, used two lines later inside
`#ifdef _MSC_VER`.

mingw-w64 installs that header as `basetsd.h`, lower case, and only that
spelling. Windows filesystems are case-insensitive, so MSVC and clang-cl
building *on Windows* never notice the mismatch. Cross-compiling with
x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc from a case-sensitive filesystem, the include is not
found and every translation unit that reaches utils.h fails:

    ../src/utils.h:28:11: fatal error: BaseTsd.h: No such file or directory

Measured against libxkbcommon 1.13.2, x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc 15.3.0, meson
cross build: 250+ of the 290 ninja targets fail this way.

mingw already provides ssize_t via <sys/types.h>, so it needs neither the
include nor the typedef -- moving the include inside the existing _MSC_VER
guard is sufficient and changes nothing for MSVC.

--- a/src/utils.h
+++ b/src/utils.h
@@ -25,7 +25,6 @@
 #ifdef _WIN32
 # include <direct.h>
 # include <io.h>
-# include <BaseTsd.h>
 # ifndef S_ISDIR
 #  define S_ISDIR(m) (((m) & S_IFMT) == S_IFDIR)
 # endif
@@ -33,6 +32,7 @@
 #  define S_ISREG(m) (((m) & S_IFMT) == S_IFREG)
 # endif
 #ifdef _MSC_VER
+# include <BaseTsd.h>
 typedef SSIZE_T ssize_t;
 #endif
 #endif
